Notebook[
 {Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["HEPCAT SYMBOL", "PacletNameCell"],
       Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["HEPCAT", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/HEPCAT"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
          ButtonBox["Related Guide", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/AmplitudeConstruction"]}],
        "AnchorBar"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.42], Scaled[0.58]}}]],
   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["CompleteHighEnergy", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Fit retained residue-preserving freedom to high-energy, spurious-pole \
and reference constraints.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"CompleteHighEnergy", "[", "input",
         ",", " ", "channels", ",", " ", "model", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     "  ",
     "Constrain a completed amplitude and its retained correction freedom."}]\
, "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"CompleteHighEnergy", "[", "input",
         ",", " ", "channels", ",", " ", "model", ",", " ", "\"Output\"",
         " ", "->", " ", "\"Details\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Insp\
ect the fit equations, affine family and independent validation."}],
   "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"],
  Cell["Pass detailed CompleteFactorization output when its remaining affine \
directions are needed. Alternatively supply a justified explicit \
\"CorrectionBasis\". Automatic uses retained information and does not create \
an unrestricted contact-operator ansatz.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The fitted directions must preserve the known physical residues. \
High-energy scaling, apparent spurious singularities and explicit reference \
dependence are tested together, and the candidate is validated again against \
the original channels.", "Notes"], Cell["The default high-energy target is \
the renormalizable tree bound E^(4-n), with masses held fixed. \
\"HighEnergyBound\" can express another stated bound; it is a physical input \
rather than an arbitrary fitting preference.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Independent high-energy validation may use a conservative all-spin \
upper-bound certificate for supported large expressions. Such a report \
records ObservedPowerUpperBound and leaves ObservedPower missing; it does not \
claim a measured leading Laurent power. Unsupported or inconclusive \
certificates retain the ordinary exact Laurent comparison.", "Notes"],
  Cell["When an exact Laurent expansion is needed, large coherent-spin \
polynomials can first be separated into all of their scalar coefficients \
without expanding the kinematic coefficient field. Every coefficient is \
expanded and reassembled exactly; no spin components or small coefficients \
are sampled away. Independent high-energy samples share one deadline and can \
run on separate workers. Large retained families can use the same exact \
coefficient separation to build fitting equations; correction unknowns are \
reassembled before extracting equations, so a condition such as x+y=0 retains \
its coupled freedom.", "Notes"], Cell["If Series assumes an exact numeric \
radical coefficient is zero, that assumption is accepted only after an exact \
algebraic zero certificate. A tiny genuine nonzero value, an unproved \
assumption, another warning or an insufficient expansion order keeps the \
result unresolved or on its original fallback. Details retain these \
certificates.", "Notes"], Cell["A successful ordinary result keeps the \
{externalMassRules, expression} form. There are no new internal on-shell \
conditions on this combined amplitude, so it may be simplified again with \
PrepareAmplitudes.", "Notes"], Cell["\"Output\" -> \"Details\" retains the \
candidate, equations, fitted family and validation. A timeout, unsupported \
direction space or unresolved free coefficient is not silently assigned an \
arbitrary value.", "Notes"], Cell["Exact identity proofs receive an allowance \
based on both the number and the size of retained affine directions. A small \
family containing a large expression can therefore receive more proof time, \
still within the stage's TimeConstraint. Details records \
FamilyIdentityProofBudget, including DirectionCount, \
LargestDirectionLeafCount and AllocatedSeconds. This changes resource \
allocation only: an unproved direction is retained, and genuine undetermined \
interactions are not discarded.", "Notes"], Cell["For a large coherent-spin \
direction whose original symbolic proof is expensive, a bounded retry factors \
numerator spectators and compacts each physical-pole group using ordinary \
identities. It keeps the original direction and the reduction route, then \
requires the existing generic symbolic external-kinematics certificate on the \
compact expression. It does not use internal shells or sampled zeros as a \
proof; an unfinished attempt retains the direction.", "Notes"],
  Cell["A late serial fallback can prove supported identities on a dense \
symbolic external rest/null chart using complete exact Laurent-polynomial \
arithmetic. It chooses angle or square null-spinor axes from the expression, \
then verifies external shells, conservation, spinor reconstruction, typed \
homogeneity, coefficient coverage and a nonzero off-cut denominator domain. \
Unit normalization requires exact mass/coupling witnesses; it is not a \
numerical phase-space test. The optional local runtime uses Python 3, a C++17 \
compiler and Boost headers. Missing tools, unsupported structure or any \
resource limit preserve the unproved direction. All preparation, compilation \
and evaluation remain inside the existing shared deadline.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Use model-local \"ParameterRules\" only for numerical sampling. An \
explicit \"RandomSeed\" replays the run; Automatic records a newly chosen \
time-based seed in details.", "Notes"], Cell["This stage cannot establish an \
unknown interaction merely because it would improve high-energy behavior. The \
model and supplied direction space determine what is being solved.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CorrectionBasis\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Explicit correction \
expressions whose coefficients may be fitted. Automatic uses bounded \
directions from the supplied diagrams, channels and retained preparation \
data; it does not invent an unrestricted interaction ansatz.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PolePreference\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Reference and \
representation preference shared by preparation and completion. Automatic \
compares or inherits admissible choices; \"AllPhysical\", \"AllSpurious\" and \
\"Mixed\" bias pole forms, while cyclic/common/independent reference choices \
and None are also available. Required checks remain unchanged.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Local numerical parameter \
overrides keyed by model references or string names. Automatic resolves the \
model's variables and dependent functions; fitting and checks do not assign \
global values or replace parameters in the symbolic final amplitude.",
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Samples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Number of physical cut \
samples or fitting samples, depending on the stage. Automatic completion \
settings choose a bounded process-dependent count; successful fitting is \
followed by separate validation samples.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ValidationSamples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Number of held-out samples \
used after fitting correction coefficients. Automatic chooses a bounded \
workload-dependent allowance; these samples are distinct from the fitting \
equations.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RandomSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Random-sampling seed. \
Automatic resolves one time-based seed for the operation; an explicit \
integer, including zero, reproduces the sample choices. Detailed reports \
retain the resolved seed. ComplicateAmplitude uses the legacy symbol key \
RandomSeed; modern construction/checking functions use the string key \
\"RandomSeed\".", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"TimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum elapsed time \
allowed by the operation or stage. Where Automatic is supported it selects a \
finite workload-dependent budget; explicit seconds or supported Infinity \
override it. A timeout is reported, never treated as a successful amplitude."\
, "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"HighEnergyBound\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum allowed power of \
energy with masses fixed. Automatic uses the renormalizable tree target \
E^(4-n); provide a justified different bound for another theory or \
normalization.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxCorrectionTerms\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Bound on the size of the \
fitted correction space. Automatic chooses a finite process-dependent limit; \
explicit values control effort without weakening residue and \
independent-validation requirements.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Parallelization\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether independent items \
or checks may use local Wolfram workers. Automatic uses suitable parallel \
work within available resources; False requests serial evaluation, and result \
order is retained.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxKernels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum local Wolfram \
worker kernels available to parallel stages. Automatic respects processor \
availability and license limits; 1 requests serial execution. Worker setup \
and expression transfer can outweigh small jobs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ValidationParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Additional or \
automatically selected local parameter assignments used in independent \
completion validation. They help detect fits tied accidentally to one \
numerical mass or coupling point without changing the symbolic result.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressReporting\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation and construction stages \
display their progress. False suppresses the live stage display without \
changing the algebra or validation.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressFunction\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Optional callback \
receiving stage progress information. Automatic uses the normal progress \
display; callbacks are evaluated on the main kernel rather than independently \
by workers.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Output\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Amplitude\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Choose the amount and \
shape of returned information. Defaults are a compact check table, prepared \
input forms, a completed {externalMassRules, expression} pair, or a bare \
constructed expression; \"Details\" preserves diagnostics and provenance.",
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment ->
      {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}}, GridBoxItemSize ->
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19], Scaled[0.58]}},
     GridBoxDividers -> {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]],
   "3ColumnTableMod"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["Basic Examples", "ExampleSection"],
  Cell[
   "Retain the factorization family and pass it into the high-energy stage.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"qedModel", " ", "=", " ",
      "ReadModel", "[", "modelDirectory", ",", " ", "2", "]", ";", "\n",
      "process", " ", "=", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ",
      "\"A.+\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", "}", ";", "\n", "diagrams", " ", "=",
      " ", "CreateDiagrams", "[", "process", ",", " ", "qedModel", "]", ";",
      "\n", "amplitudes", " ", "=", " ", "diagramAmplitudes", "[",
      "diagrams", "]", ";", "\n", "channels", " ", "=", " ",
      "FactorizationAmplitudeChannels", "[", "process", ",", " ", "qedModel",
      "]", ";", "\n", "prepared", " ", "=", " ", "PrepareAmplitudes", "[",
      "amplitudes", ",", " ", "qedModel", ",", " ", "\"ReturnDetails\"", " ",
      "->", " ", "True", "]", ";", "\n", "factorized", " ", "=", " ",
      "CompleteFactorization", "[", "prepared", ",", " ", "channels", ",",
      " ", "qedModel", ",", " ", "\"ReturnDetails\"", " ", "->", " ", "True",
      "]", ";", "\n", "CompleteHighEnergy", "[", "factorized", ",", " ",
      "channels", ",", " ", "qedModel", ",", " ", "\"Output\"", " ", "->",
      " ", "\"Details\"", "]"}]], "Input"], Cell["This example writes files, \
starts a longer calculation, or requires an optional external tool. Evaluate \
it when you want to perform that operation.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell["Retain an allowed four-point scalar contact interaction.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"scalarModel", " ", "=", " ", "{",
      "{", "{", "\"scalar\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ",
      "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",",
      " ", "\"\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", "}", "}", ",", " ",
      "{", "{", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ",
      "\"s\"", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "7", "}", "}", ",", " ", "{", "}",
      ",", " ", "{", "}", "}", ";", "\n", "externalRules", " ", "=", " ",
      "Thread", "[", "(", "Mass", " ", "/@", " ", "Range", "[", "4", "]",
